					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607504129" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607222771 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 02:46</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837525">
									

<p>The problem is that seems to be just a single instance of a shellshocked soldier. With that as a given, there's little of interest here. You need to build more into the character than that; if he could be treated then he may give some interesting historical notes, even possibly describe the SCP that transported him through time.</p>
<p>Or he could have the ability to time travel himself, and the ability was triggered due to stress. even if it was a one-time ability, it could be fascinating to study him. If it's not, then he could be of help in exploring historical eras, possibly confirming details.</p>
<p>If you are going to keep him shellshocked, then you need to show what he can add to the knowledge of The Foundation. There has to be some sign of what caused him to time travel or it's just a neat idea.</p>
<p>In what seems to be a common theme today, this is just the beginning of an idea, and needs to be fleshed out somewhat or it's just The Foundation equivalent of a freak; he's going to be confined until he dies, possibly gets killed, and not really contribute anything.</p>

							</div>

								
					
